\title{rdmrtmb: Frequentist Estimation of the Racing Diffusion Model}
\description{
Maximum likelihood estimation of the racing diffusion model of speeded
decision making. Every model parameter can be described by its own model
matrix, and random effects can be specified per parameter with lme4-style
terms such as \code{(1 | id)}. Random effects are integrated with the Laplace
approximation using automatic differentiation provided by RTMB.
}
\details{
The drift rates of a race model necessarily differ between the accumulators:
each response alternative accumulates evidence at its own rate. The remaining
parameters (the start point range \code{A}, the threshold \code{b}, the non-decision
time \code{t0} and the diffusion constant \code{s}) are properties of the race as a
whole and are shared by the accumulators unless a term is placed inside
\code{acc()}. \code{b = ~ acc(1)} gives one threshold per accumulator, which is a
response bias, and \code{v = ~ Condition + acc(.acc == Word)} adds one coefficient
that compares the accumulator with a trial variable; see \code{\link[=acc]{acc()}}.
}
